rm_and_Pelton_Basin_seen_from_Cascade_Pass_(52313782653).jpg","dist_m":153,"width":640,"height":316,"license":"CC BY 2.0","license_url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/2.0","artist":"lamblukas from San Francisco, United States"}],"street":null},{"id":"way/847355131","name":"Copper Mountain Fire Lookout","kind":"historic","lon":-121.46263,"lat":48.90845,"ele_m":null,"wikidata":"Q5168754","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Copper_Mountain_Fire_Lookout","tour":1,"summary":{"extract":"The Copper Mountain Fire Lookout was built in 1934 in what was then the Glacier Ranger district of Mount Baker National Forest. The cabin-like wood frame lookout is a frame cabin with large windows on each side protected by an awning-style shutter. A shingled gable roof with prominent lightning rods covers the cabin. The lookout measures 14.25 feet (4.34 m) by 14.25 feet (4.34 m) square. During the winter of 1943 the lookout was staffed by the Aircraft Warning Service and used to watch for enemy aircraft. It is one of three lookouts remaining in North Cascades National Park from the Forest Service administration.","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Copper_Mountain_Fire_Lookout","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","attribution":"Wikipedia"},"photos":[],"street":null},{"id":"node/9109865186","name":"Rock Cabin","kind":"historic","lon":-120.99765,"lat":48.57821,"ele_m":null,"wikidata":"Q17194318","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rock_Cabin","tour":4,"summary":{"extract":"The Rock Cabin is in North Cascades National Park, in the U.S. state of Washington. Constructed by trapper John Dayo in the 1920s, the cabin was placed on the National Register of Historic Places in 1989.","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rock_Cabin","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","attribution":"Wikipedia"},"photos":[],"street":null},{"id":"way/372628985","name":"Sourdough Mountain Lookout","kind":"historic","lon":-121.10955,"lat":48.74271,"ele_m":null,"wikidata":"Q17184058","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sourdough_